			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Generalize hardcoded volume paths in comments\n\nReplace literal `/Volumes/CORSAIR/...` and `/Users/nikola/...` references with abstract placeholders (`<vol>`, `<home>`) across build, utility, and effect modules.\n\nUpdate comments in `Scheme.rs`, `WindowBuild.rs`, `PathSecurity.rs`, and `FileSystem.rs` to reflect generic path structures rather than local development environment specifics. This ensures documentation accuracy regardless of the developer's mount points or home directory structure, aligning with the project's requirement for portable, environment-agnostic logging and comments.\n\nNo functional code changes were introduced; only documentation strings were updated to prevent confusion during future maintenance or code review.",
			"SHA": "4dd712f4d78aad6976cb327b861e369409817a36"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:35:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1492,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Update documentation and telemetry configuration for v2.2\n\nSync CHANGELOG.md and README.md to reflect the v2.2 correctness pass, detailing the reduction of Cocoon circuit-breaker rejections to zero via the new `-32004` JSON-RPC error code for benign 404s. Expand documentation on the `sky:replay-events` handler, terminal ring buffers, and the modularization of the IPC layer.\n\nIn `build.rs`, propagate new OTLP telemetry environment variables (`OTLPEndpoint`, `OTLPEnabled`, `Capture`, `Trace`) to the compilation target, enabling granular trace filtering and endpoint configuration. Update `scripts/cocoon/bootstrap-fork.js` to emit structured OTLP spans for bootstrap milestones, aligning the extension host instrumentation with the new backend tracing capabilities. Minor formatting adjustments applied to `capabilities/default.json`.",
			"SHA": "5bca3dde328711d9c6f263697f20d507a847c0cf"
		}
	],
